# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE, AND WHY
#
# This repository holds the PRODUCT (the four starters, the evaluation harness, the docs and
# findings) — not the EVIDENCE. Stored results are 129G and cannot live on a remote; they are
# backed up separately, see tasks/12.
#
# Nothing here is "temporary files". Each entry is either build output that regenerates, or
# evidence too large to push. If you add an entry, say which.

# ---- stored evidence: 129G. Backed up separately, never pushed. -------------------------
eval/runs/
staging/

# ---- build output, regenerates from source --------------------------------------------
**/node_modules/
**/target/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/artifacts/
**/coverage/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Unity: Library/ is a multi-GB import cache, Temp/ and obj/ are per-build.
# Assets/Analyzers/*.dll is NOT ignored — the analyzer binaries are part of the template.
**/Library/
**/Temp/
**/obj/
**/Logs/
**/MemoryCaptures/
**/UserSettings/
*.csproj
*.sln

# Godot import cache
**/.godot/
**/*.import

# Python envs
.venv/
venv/

# ---- machine-local, not shared ---------------------------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json
.DS_Store

# Per-agent git worktrees. One-agent-per-task creates a checkout per agent under here;
# committing them would put one agent's entire working copy inside another's history,
# and `git add -A` in a wind-down would do it silently.
.claude/worktrees/

# ---- retired trees: nothing under here may be tracked again ----------------------------
#
# The four template*/ trees were deleted 2026-08-23 (DECISIONS.md, #122). The deletion commit
# was complete — zero template*/ paths — and the MERGE re-added five, because each tree carried
# its own .gitignore covering its build output (template-ts/.gitignore ignored `public/main.js`
# and `.eslintcache`; template-unity/.gitignore ignored `/tools/analyzer/bin/`). Deleting a tree
# deletes its ignore rules, so every build artefact still on disk under it became visible to
# `git add -A`, and the merge swept in an eslint cache, a 1.2M bundle and a compiled analyzer
# with its .pdb. AGENTS.md then stated `template*/ is deleted` while 5 paths were tracked.
#
# This entry exists so that a leftover build tree in an old checkout cannot be re-committed.
# It is scoped to `template*/` on purpose: a general `**/bin/` rule would also ignore
# eval/starters/rust/crates/{game,sim}/src/bin/, which is Rust source.
template*/
